  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-disk-space.test.ts --run
  node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor-lint.test.ts --run

Why the integration case matters:
- the collector unit case proves explicit env beats ambient process.env;
- the selected-check case proves the registered contribution receives operator/source env while plugin inspection remains isolated;
- source SQLite bytes remain unchanged.

Compatibility:
- no config key change;
- no persisted schema change;
- no migration/backfill;
- no state write;
- noteDiskSpace() keeps its existing ambient process.env behavior;
- only the structured Doctor health-check path gains explicit source-env ownership.

Self-check notes (2026-10-07):
- current doctor-disk-space.test.ts already imports * as diskSpace and spies on tryReadDiskSpace;
- tryReadDiskSpace(targetPath: string) returns the exact snapshot shape used above;
- current helper signatures accept resolveRequiredHomeDir(env, os.homedir) and resolveStateDir(env, homedir);
- current mixed-selected-check test already owns stateDir/databasePath/sourceOpenStacks and source SQLite preservation assertions;
- this artifact remains source-reviewed, not executed.

